# Trivy exceptions for the release CRITICAL gate.
#
# Policy (PERS-56 ADR-006): Trivy blocks publication on a CRITICAL finding that
# has a fix available (ignore-unfixed is enabled, so unfixed base-image CVEs do
# not block). A temporary exception is allowed only as an entry below with:
#   - the CVE id,
#   - an owner,
#   - an expiry date that Security Auditor reviews,
#   - the reason a fix is deferred.
# Entries without an owner and expiry must be rejected in review. Remove the
# entry when the fix ships or the expiry passes.
#
# Example (do not uncomment without an owner and expiry):
# CVE-0000-00000  # owner: @maintainer, expires: 2026-12-31, reason: ...
